---
description: Rails migrations (change, backfills SQL, commentaires en français au-dessus du SQL)
globs:
  - "db/migrate/**/*.rb"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Migrations

- Prefer `change` over `up` / `down`. In production we almost never roll back; we add follow-up migrations. Rollback is mainly for local dev when something fails.
- Data backfills / fixes: use **SQL** (`execute`, etc.), not ActiveRecord models (`User.update_all`, `find_each`, …). Keep statements tight and index-friendly to reduce locks / long transactions.
- Above every SQL statement: a **short, clear comment in French** so reviewers see intent and can sanity-check production behavior.
- SQL that must run only on migrate-up inside `change`: use `up_only` so the rest of the migration stays reversible.
